  "prefLabel": "Psyc 306.01 Jurisprudence Examination",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Psyc 306.01 Jurisprudence Examination.\n\n(a) Each applicant for initial licensure or reinstatement of licensure shall be examined on the contents of RSA 329-B psychologists practice act and Psyc 100 through Psyc 500.\n\n(b) The examination shall be developed by the board of psychology and administered by the OPLC through a third party that has been contracted by the OPLC.\n\n(c) The exam shall be as follows:\n\n(1) Open book using a study guide supplied by the board;\n\n(2) Available on a secure website; and\n\n(3) Taken individually without consulting others.\n\n(d) An individual shall achieve a passing score of at least 80 percent.\n\n(e) An individual who fails the jurisprudence examination may re-take the examination as many times as it takes the individual to pass.\n\nSource. #14569, eff 6-30-26, EXPIRES: 6-30-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/psyc100-500.html"
